# The board bundles are generated output: `pnpm build:board` reproduces every
# one of them from `packages/board/`. They are minified — a few lines of many
# thousands of characters each — so git's line-based merge lands every board
# change in the same handful of enormous lines. Two branches touching entirely
# disjoint sources still collide there, and the resulting diff cannot be read,
# let alone resolved.
#
# `-merge` tells git not to blend the two versions. It keeps one side whole and
# reports the conflict, WITHOUT writing conflict markers into the file. The
# artifact therefore stays valid, buildable JavaScript through a conflict, and
# the resolution is to rebuild rather than to read:
#
#     git checkout --ours skills/plot/scripts/board/board-server.mjs   # either side
#     pnpm build:board
#     git add skills/plot/scripts/board/board-server.mjs
#
# Which side you keep cannot matter, because the rebuild overwrites it. Do not
# phrase the resolution as "take ours": under `git merge` ours is the branch
# being merged into, under `git rebase` it is the upstream, and this repo
# rebases routinely.
#
# This is an attribute, not a custom merge driver (`merge=rebuild`), on purpose.
# `.gitattributes` is versioned and travels with the repo; a driver DEFINITION
# lives in each clone's `git config`, so on CI and fresh clones the attribute
# would name a driver that does not exist and git would silently fall back to a
# normal merge. See docs/definition-of-done.md › Resolving a board artifact
# conflict.
#
# The CI no-diff gate is what keeps this honest: resolve by keeping a stale
# artifact and forget to rebuild, and the build fails.
#
# THE LIST IS THE BUILD'S OUTPUT, not one file. It named `board-server.mjs`
# alone until 2026-09-06, while `build.mjs` grew eight more outputs and none of
# them arrived here. Measured on one rebase, 2026-09-05: the marked file took
# zero conflict markers, `plot-ask.mjs` took five and `plot-registryd.mjs` took
# three — spliced into generated output that is committable, pushable, and not
# JavaScript. `scripts/check-bundle-attributes.sh` now derives this set from
# `build.mjs` and fails when one is missing, because a list nothing checks is a
# list the next author does not know exists.
#
# `plot-monitor.mjs` IS ABSENT DELIBERATELY. It is tracked and documented at
# `entry/monitor.ts:14`, and it appears in no `outfile` — nothing rebuilds it.
# The licence for `-merge` is the deterministic rebuild, since "keep either
# side, then rebuild" is safe only where the rebuild overwrites what was kept.
# Marking it would assert a rebuild that does not exist.
skills/plot/scripts/board/board-server.mjs -merge
skills/plot/scripts/board/plot-ask.mjs -merge
skills/plot/scripts/board/plot-delta.mjs -merge
skills/plot/scripts/board/plot-landed.mjs -merge
skills/plot/scripts/board/plot-movable.mjs -merge
skills/plot/scripts/board/plot-prompt.mjs -merge
skills/plot/scripts/board/plot-registryd.mjs -merge
skills/plot/scripts/board/plot-standing.mjs -merge
skills/plot/scripts/board/plot-task.mjs -merge
skills/plot/scripts/board/plot-transition.mjs -merge
skills/plot/scripts/board/plot-verdicts.mjs -merge
